;; spec:   stdlib §4.3 (row print-method: an impl for the type), §2.3 (one impl per head), §2.7 (three printers)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  overlapping instances: Debug for i64 is already implemented
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: print-method
;; `print-method` is the static form of the extension point, an `impl Debug T` and an `impl Show T`, and
;; it is the instance of a type the program defines. Clojure's own use of it, redefining how a built-in
;; type prints, is refused here: the library already has `Debug i64`, and a type has one instance of a
;; protocol (a second is an overlap; case 2956 shows the way round, a wrapper type of the program's own).
;; The message names the protocol and the type, so the program sees which library instance it ran into.
(ns main)

(impl Debug i64 (debug (self) "mine"))

(defun main () -> i64 (do (prn 1) 0))
